<b>Racer Profile!</b>

00:05:59.850 --> 00:06:02.210
<b>Racer Profile!</b>

00:05:59.850 --> 00:06:02.210
<b>Mihono</b>

00:05:59.850 --> 00:06:02.210
<b>Bourbon</b>

00:06:02.760 --> 00:06:05.960
<i>She's been undefeated at both the 
Satsukishou and the Derby, after all.</i>

00:06:05.960 --> 00:06:07.740
<i>I think she'll put on a great
 show at the Kikkashou.</i>

00:06:08.180 --> 00:06:12.330
<i>We might actually see a horse girl win 
the Triple Crown while undefeated!</i>

00:06:12.330 --> 00:06:14.230
<i>Autumn's races are shaping 
up to be must-sees.</i>

00:06:14.230 --> 00:06:17.180
<i>And now, a special profile on the 
star horse girl, Mihono Bourbon.</i>

00:06:22.650 --> 00:06:26.990
Mihono Bourbon

00:06:22.650 --> 00:06:26.990
<b>The Incline Prodigy</b>

00:06:22.650 --> 00:06:34.950
<b>Umamusume Tariku</b>

00:06:24.230 --> 00:06:26.550
<i>This horse girl's morning starts early.</i>

00:06:27.830 --> 00:06:30.480
<i>She never misses her daily training.</i>

00:06:30.480 --> 00:06:32.690
<i>It's natural that I work hard.</i>

00:06:31.590 --> 00:06:34.950
<b>Onto
an
Undefeated
Triple
Crown...</b>

00:06:32.690 --> 00:06:36.220
<i>And winning is equally natural.</i>

00:06:38.910 --> 00:06:43.670
Aim to be an undefeated Triple Crown horse girl! {now entirely crossed out}

00:06:40.450 --> 00:06:42.770
An undefeated Triple Crown, huh?

00:06:49.250 --> 00:06:51.000
I've finally come this far.

00:06:51.800 --> 00:06:53.980
I know you're there, Rice.

00:06:56.930 --> 00:07:00.280
The Triple Crown that even 
Tokai Teio-san was unable to achieve...

00:06:56.970 --> 00:07:00.500
<b>R
i
c
e
 
S
h
o
w
e
r</b>

00:07:00.280 --> 00:07:02.190
I will make it a reality.

00:07:02.580 --> 00:07:05.480
Those are Master's orders, 
and I will obey them.

00:07:13.550 --> 00:07:15.870
What the hell am I supposed to do?!

00:07:15.870 --> 00:07:17.050
Maybe drink less.

00:07:17.050 --> 00:07:20.060
I just want her to look forward again.

00:07:20.060 --> 00:07:22.480
So I busted my butt for her training plan!

00:07:22.480 --> 00:07:25.020
I tried to come up with the 
best possible race plan, too!

00:07:25.020 --> 00:07:25.920
But...

00:07:25.920 --> 00:07:27.010
She's been "fine."

00:07:27.010 --> 00:07:30.160
Right! She's been doing a 
"fine" job of everything!

00:07:30.160 --> 00:07:32.230
But there's not a hint of the old Teio spark!

00:07:32.230 --> 00:07:35.690
I know her passion for 
racing can't be gone.

00:07:35.690 --> 00:07:36.890
But...

00:07:36.890 --> 00:07:38.550
What am I supposed to do?!

00:07:38.550 --> 00:07:39.780
Unbelievable.

00:07:39.780 --> 00:07:41.300
I'm also broke.

00:07:41.810 --> 00:07:43.270
Get a grip, would you?!

00:07:44.520 --> 00:07:49.110
You managed to work through Tokai Teio's 
injury at the derby, didn't you?

00:07:49.320 --> 00:07:50.560
But...

00:07:50.560 --> 00:07:53.310
But she couldn't achieve 
her Triple Crown dream,

00:07:53.310 --> 00:07:55.810
and her dream of being 
undefeated is gone now, too.

00:07:55.810 --> 00:07:57.230
Do you realize how few horse girls

00:07:57.230 --> 00:08:00.720
can make their dreams from before 
they start racing a reality?

00:08:01.210 --> 00:08:04.290
And dreams can take different 
shapes over time.

00:08:05.490 --> 00:08:09.020
If she can get through this, 
Tokai Teio will be even stronger.

00:08:10.340 --> 00:08:13.300
You need to have some faith 
in her in the meantime.

00:08:13.300 --> 00:08:14.610
Ow, ow, ow...

00:08:14.610 --> 00:08:15.720
I'm heading out.

00:08:16.460 --> 00:08:18.180
Thank you for coming by.

00:08:19.260 --> 00:08:20.280
Thanks.

00:08:26.280 --> 00:08:27.260
Bartender...

00:08:27.260 --> 00:08:28.150
Yes?

00:08:28.400 --> 00:08:30.440
You got any glasses that need washing?

00:08:32.860 --> 00:08:35.130
There's quite a few to go 
to cover your tab, you know.

00:08:35.130 --> 00:08:36.870
I've got it handled!

00:08:36.870 --> 00:08:40.140
<i>Teio, I'm gonna make sure 
you make your comeback!</i>

00:08:42.330 --> 00:08:44.540
Bourbon-san!

00:08:43.350 --> 00:08:44.540
You can do it!

00:08:44.540 --> 00:08:45.480
Come on!

00:08:45.480 --> 00:08:47.040
Go, Bourbon!

00:08:48.030 --> 00:08:49.500
<i>Mihono Bourbon is out in front!</i>

00:08:49.500 --> 00:08:52.290
<i>Rice Shower is moving up, 
along with Machikane Tannhäuser!</i>

00:08:52.290 --> 00:08:53.970
<i>Mihono Bourbon is maintaining a narrow lead!</i>

00:08:53.970 --> 00:08:55.390
<i>But Rice Shower closing in on the outside!</i>

00:08:55.390 --> 00:08:56.680
<i>Machikane Tannhäuser moves up the inside!</i>

00:08:56.680 --> 00:08:58.250
<i>Rice Shower and Tannhäuser!</i>

00:08:58.250 --> 00:08:59.530
<i>Rice Shower's taken the lead!</i>

00:08:59.530 --> 00:09:00.640
<i>And she takes the goal!</i>

00:09:00.240 --> 00:09:00.640
Kikkashou

00:09:01.400 --> 00:09:04.640
<i>Mihono Bourbon is unable 
to claim her Triple Crown!</i>

00:09:02.620 --> 00:09:04.640
Are you kidding me?!

00:09:04.640 --> 00:09:07.600
<i>The Kikkashou's winning 
horse girl is Rice Shower!</i>

00:09:15.080 --> 00:09:17.410
Wait, what?

00:09:17.410 --> 00:09:19.990
Unfortunately, you lost your 
chance at the Triple Crown.

00:09:20.220 --> 00:09:21.080
Yes.

00:09:21.080 --> 00:09:23.750
I'm sorry I was unable to live 
up to Master's expectations.

00:09:23.750 --> 00:09:27.120
But, I believe I have 
gained something in this loss.

00:09:27.120 --> 00:09:28.630
<i>Next time, I will win.</i>

00:09:28.630 --> 00:09:30.990
<i>Uh, Bourbon-san? Wait!</i>

00:09:31.730 --> 00:09:34.490
Gain something... by losing?

00:09:34.970 --> 00:09:38.970
<b>Umamusume</b>

00:09:34.970 --> 00:09:38.970
<b><i>Pretty Derby</i></b>

00:09:41.200 --> 00:09:43.930
Mejiro Palmer and Daitaku Helios are 
seriously outrunning the competition.

00:09:43.930 --> 00:09:46.780
There are ten lengths between them 
and the third-place runner!

00:09:46.780 --> 00:09:51.400
They'll need to close in soon to stand 
any chance against the two in the lead!

00:09:51.710 --> 00:09:54.410
Is Tokai Teio going to be 
all right in her position?

00:09:54.410 --> 00:09:58.020
She's had a lot of big ups and 
downs in her races recently.

00:09:58.020 --> 00:09:59.350
It's a bit worrying.

00:09:59.850 --> 00:10:02.830
<i>Ow... I think I hit my rear 
on the way out of the gate.</i>

00:10:03.990 --> 00:10:06.500
<i>I can't win the Triple 
Crown or be undefeated.</i>

00:10:06.500 --> 00:10:08.750
<i>I can't be like the Prez anymore.</i>

00:10:08.750 --> 00:10:11.880
<i>So why am I even running anymore?</i>

00:10:13.670 --> 00:10:15.040
Let's go, Helios!

00:10:15.040 --> 00:10:15.460
Yo!

00:10:15.460 --> 00:10:17.340
Come on!

00:10:20.890 --> 00:10:23.290
<i>Why are they trying so hard?</i>

00:10:24.410 --> 00:10:27.560
Tokai Teio is remaining steady, 
five to six positions from the rear.

00:10:27.560 --> 00:10:30.550
I don't think Teio-san's 
feeling well yet.

00:10:30.550 --> 00:10:31.810
No, this is fine.

00:10:31.810 --> 00:10:34.450
How, exactly?! Can't you 
see how far back she is?!

00:10:34.450 --> 00:10:37.660
There are things you can only 
learn by running in a race.

00:10:38.540 --> 00:10:41.280
<i>You need to use this chance 
to figure it out, Teio!</i>

00:10:42.480 --> 00:10:45.250
<i>If I move further up, will I understand?</i>

00:10:46.130 --> 00:10:48.520
<i>Why the others are running?</i>

00:10:49.240 --> 00:10:52.440
<i>And why I should run?</i>

00:10:52.440 --> 00:10:55.680
Coming around the fourth corner, 
and Mejiro Palmer is going for it.

00:10:55.680 --> 00:10:58.800
There's a 310 meter straightaway left, 
with the Nakayama course being a short one.

00:10:58.800 --> 00:11:00.260
You've got this!

00:11:00.260 --> 00:11:03.050
We're BFFs!

00:11:00.550 --> 00:11:03.050
Lyric Earth is moving 
up and narrowing the lead!

00:11:03.050 --> 00:11:04.620
And Nice Nature is closing 
in from the outside!

00:11:04.620 --> 00:11:07.680
And Mejiro Palmer and 
Lyric Earth cross the goal!

00:11:09.890 --> 00:11:13.560
Oh yeah! I did it! Helios!

00:11:21.950 --> 00:11:23.820
Nice job, Ikuno!

00:11:22.360 --> 00:11:25.240
Congratulations on third place, Nature-san!

00:11:37.550 --> 00:11:38.990
I couldn't make it.

00:11:39.790 --> 00:11:42.350
Teio-san... in 11th place?

00:11:42.350 --> 00:11:43.630
Oh, damn.

00:11:43.630 --> 00:11:46.120
I thought it was supposed to work out.

00:11:46.120 --> 00:11:47.450
I've got somewhere to be.

00:11:47.450 --> 00:11:48.800
Where are you going?

00:11:48.800 --> 00:11:50.490
Let him go, Spe.

00:11:50.490 --> 00:11:51.270
But...

00:11:55.100 --> 00:11:56.360
Ow, ow, ow...

00:11:57.630 --> 00:11:58.850
<i>Damn it.</i>

00:12:04.760 --> 00:12:09.040
I thought I had lost everything, but...

00:12:09.610 --> 00:12:14.440
I'm glad... I can still be 
frustrated after losing.

00:12:16.630 --> 00:12:20.580
Damn it! Damn it!

00:12:20.580 --> 00:12:21.550
Good.

00:12:22.470 --> 00:12:24.930
<b>TOKAI TEIO INJURED</b>

00:12:24.930 --> 00:12:26.890
<b>TOKAI TEIO INJURED</b>

00:12:28.640 --> 00:12:30.600
<b>Tokai Teio Injured Again!</b>

00:12:30.600 --> 00:12:32.600
<b>Tokai Teio Injured!
Injury to Left Gluteus Medius Will Require Protracted Rehab</b>

00:12:32.860 --> 00:12:34.390
What exactly is this?

00:12:34.390 --> 00:12:37.360
You get to be Spica's team leader!

00:12:34.390 --> 00:12:38.610
<b>I am the leader</b>

00:12:37.360 --> 00:12:38.610
Leader?

00:12:38.610 --> 00:12:40.580
That's right. From now on, you're going to be

00:12:40.580 --> 00:12:44.070
supporting the rest of 
the team as its leader.

00:12:45.120 --> 00:12:47.450
So I'm not a racer anymore?

00:12:48.160 --> 00:12:51.040
Are you trying to say 
I don't need to run anymore?

00:12:51.040 --> 00:12:52.040
No, no!

00:12:52.040 --> 00:12:55.510
There are some things you can only figure out 
by working to help others, that's all.

00:12:55.510 --> 00:12:57.470
I don't even know what you're talking about.

00:12:57.470 --> 00:12:58.940
Now, hang on!

00:12:58.940 --> 00:13:02.770
This is something that you'll need 
to start winning races again!

00:13:02.770 --> 00:13:04.740
Win... races?

00:13:05.380 --> 00:13:09.570
It's the kind of thing that you can't 
really understand without doing it.

00:13:09.570 --> 00:13:11.850
Come on! Think of it as an 
experiment or something.

00:13:14.680 --> 00:13:16.600
So what am I supposed to do?

00:13:17.400 --> 00:13:20.110
Sweets! Sweets! Sweets!

00:13:25.360 --> 00:13:27.910
Why am I doing this?

00:13:27.910 --> 00:13:30.570
Whoa, this one's a total mess!

00:13:31.030 --> 00:13:34.040
<b>Spe's</b>

00:13:38.500 --> 00:13:41.290
Am I seriously supposed to make this many?

00:13:42.100 --> 00:13:44.550
Then again, I guess I ate a bunch, too.

00:13:45.170 --> 00:13:46.880
Vodka's

00:13:46.880 --> 00:13:49.850
Why's Vodka got so many towels?!

00:13:51.040 --> 00:13:52.310
Leader!

00:13:52.310 --> 00:13:55.270
D.S.'S

00:13:52.750 --> 00:13:55.270
Ugh, that's even more than Vodka's!

00:13:55.270 --> 00:13:57.960
Hey, is being a leader really about 
doing a bunch of crummy chores?!

00:13:57.960 --> 00:13:59.520
Hey, they're not crummy at all.

00:13:59.520 --> 00:14:02.110
Horseshoes, diet, laundry...

00:14:02.110 --> 00:14:04.940
It's all stuff necessary to run well.

00:14:06.400 --> 00:14:09.700
Once you're done, go check 
the others out as they run,

00:14:09.700 --> 00:14:10.970
Leader.

00:14:12.250 --> 00:14:14.400
I'm not sure I buy any of this.

00:14:19.350 --> 00:14:21.100
Trainer, I finished...

00:14:21.100 --> 00:14:22.130
Kick it up a notch!

00:14:32.250 --> 00:14:34.010
Good! Nice times.

00:14:36.000 --> 00:14:37.780
I won that time.

00:14:37.780 --> 00:14:39.270
No, me!

00:14:39.270 --> 00:14:41.070
Go get hydrated!

00:14:41.070 --> 00:14:43.070
Leader, could you hand them their drinks?

00:14:43.070 --> 00:14:44.450
Oh, okay.

00:14:44.450 --> 00:14:46.400
Spe, Golshi, you're next!

00:14:46.400 --> 00:14:47.250
Okay!

00:14:47.250 --> 00:14:48.320
You got it.

00:14:51.690 --> 00:14:53.140
I feel alive again!

00:14:53.140 --> 00:14:54.860
I know that I won just now.

00:14:54.860 --> 00:14:57.540
Give it a rest! I was faster!

00:14:58.830 --> 00:15:01.070
What do you think, Leader?!

00:15:01.070 --> 00:15:02.460
Hey...

00:15:02.870 --> 00:15:06.170
What are you two racing for?

00:15:06.170 --> 00:15:07.690
To beat her!

00:15:07.690 --> 00:15:09.130
Stop copying me!

00:15:09.130 --> 00:15:10.070
I'm not!

00:15:10.070 --> 00:15:11.390
But think about it.

00:15:11.390 --> 00:15:14.290
It's not like you're always gonna 
be in the same races, right?

00:15:14.290 --> 00:15:15.960
What about the rest of the time?

00:15:15.960 --> 00:15:18.730
Oh, that doesn't matter at all.

00:15:18.990 --> 00:15:21.560
I'd definitely win if it was the same race.

00:15:21.560 --> 00:15:24.310
But the other races still matter.

00:15:24.670 --> 00:15:28.980
That's right! You better bust your butt 
all the time if you want to beat me.

00:15:28.980 --> 00:15:30.640
I could say the same thing!

00:15:30.640 --> 00:15:32.550
Beating you is easy mode!

00:15:32.550 --> 00:15:35.070
Well beating you, Vodka, is super easy mode!

00:15:33.990 --> 00:15:37.330
Come on, quit fighting!

00:15:37.640 --> 00:15:40.260
Do you suppose Leader-san 
is going to be okay?

00:15:40.260 --> 00:15:42.540
She's trying to find something.

00:15:41.450 --> 00:15:44.640
Beating you is super-duper-uber easy mode!

00:15:42.540 --> 00:15:44.640
Her reason for racing.

00:15:44.640 --> 00:15:47.800
Well beating you is super-mega-
ultra-hyper-max easy mode!

00:15:45.520 --> 00:15:47.140
Her reason for racing?

00:15:52.440 --> 00:15:54.680
Looks like everything's ready.

00:16:06.800 --> 00:16:09.060
Where the heck am I?

00:16:09.550 --> 00:16:11.400
<b>Here</b>

00:16:09.550 --> 00:16:11.400
<b>Road</b>

00:16:09.550 --> 00:16:11.400
<b>Tracen
 Academy</b>

00:16:10.950 --> 00:16:12.060
And what's this?

00:16:12.060 --> 00:16:13.530
A mission for our leader.

00:16:14.250 --> 00:16:15.870
I seriously don't get any of this.

00:16:15.870 --> 00:16:17.090
You will if you go.

00:16:17.090 --> 00:16:19.840
And remember, you're headed 
there as team leader.

00:16:19.840 --> 00:16:22.440
So make sure to keep that sash on.

00:16:25.210 --> 00:16:27.280
<i>This has to be a prank.</i>

00:16:27.280 --> 00:16:28.460
Excuse me—

00:16:28.460 --> 00:16:31.260
I'm not wearing it because 
I want to, I swear!

00:16:31.260 --> 00:16:32.930
You're Tokai Teio-san, right?

00:16:40.260 --> 00:16:41.540
Y-Yes.

00:16:41.540 --> 00:16:42.930
I knew it!

00:16:42.930 --> 00:16:45.080
I'm always rooting for you!

00:16:45.080 --> 00:16:47.080
Um, can I shake your hand?

00:16:47.930 --> 00:16:49.240
O-Okay...

00:16:49.800 --> 00:16:51.430
Thank you so much!

00:16:51.430 --> 00:16:53.240
I have something to brag 
to my friends about now.

00:16:54.410 --> 00:16:57.450
I'm curious, what are you the leader of?

00:16:57.450 --> 00:16:59.990
I-It's nothing, really!

00:17:02.000 --> 00:17:04.460
<b>PARK VIEWING PLATFORM</b>

00:17:02.570 --> 00:17:03.800
See you!

00:17:09.320 --> 00:17:12.170
Seriously, where am I?

00:17:16.830 --> 00:17:18.640
I've been awaiting your arrival.

00:17:20.220 --> 00:17:21.600
Butler-san?!

00:17:22.230 --> 00:17:26.190
Leader-sama, thank you 
for coming all this way.

00:17:26.190 --> 00:17:29.040
You scared me! I didn't 
recognize you at first.

00:17:29.040 --> 00:17:31.520
And you're calling me "Leader" too, huh?

00:17:31.520 --> 00:17:34.010
Right this way, Leader-sama.

00:17:40.290 --> 00:17:43.340
Uh, where are we going?

00:17:44.520 --> 00:17:46.020
Um...

00:17:46.020 --> 00:17:47.340
It's over there.

00:17:51.210 --> 00:17:53.330
What is this place?

00:17:54.340 --> 00:17:57.470
The Mejiro family's sanatorium.

00:17:59.120 --> 00:18:00.450
Um...

00:18:01.610 --> 00:18:02.990
Well...

00:18:03.640 --> 00:18:06.140
I'm not sure why I'm here.

00:18:10.590 --> 00:18:12.510
The young miss is expecting you.

00:18:19.360 --> 00:18:20.790
McQueen?

00:18:22.130 --> 00:18:25.100
Miss, I've brought Leader-sama to see you.

00:18:25.100 --> 00:18:27.220
Excellent work, Butler.

00:18:27.220 --> 00:18:29.780
Teio, one moment, please.

00:18:29.780 --> 00:18:31.290
R-Right.

00:18:31.960 --> 00:18:33.840
Ten more to go.

00:18:44.010 --> 00:18:45.970
<b>I am the leader</b>

00:18:46.890 --> 00:18:49.100
How are your injuries?

00:18:49.100 --> 00:18:53.540
Quite well. I'll be rejoining Spica shortly.

00:18:53.540 --> 00:18:56.780
I think I've gained muscle that 
will help with my running.

00:18:57.250 --> 00:18:58.950
I-I see.

00:19:09.980 --> 00:19:11.040
McQueen...

00:19:11.270 --> 00:19:12.650
What is it?

00:19:12.650 --> 00:19:17.110
McQueen, how can you... 
Why do you try so hard?

00:19:17.550 --> 00:19:21.150
Because I am only looking at my goal.

00:19:21.150 --> 00:19:22.040
Your goal?

00:19:22.510 --> 00:19:26.130
Currently, it's to become stronger 
than I was before my injury.

00:19:26.130 --> 00:19:29.980
After that, it will be defeating 
a certain opponent.

00:19:29.980 --> 00:19:32.000
I can't afford to dawdle.

00:19:32.800 --> 00:19:35.360
I didn't know you had someone like that.

00:19:35.360 --> 00:19:36.920
Is it strange?

00:19:36.920 --> 00:19:40.070
Well, you blew everyone 
away at the Tennoushou.

00:19:40.070 --> 00:19:43.170
They're calling you the 
greatest stayer in history!

00:19:43.170 --> 00:19:45.860
Who could you still want to beat?

00:19:45.860 --> 00:19:50.470
It's having someone I want to defeat 
that allows me to become stronger.

00:19:50.470 --> 00:19:51.410
Stronger?

00:19:51.410 --> 00:19:52.840
Much stronger.

00:19:53.310 --> 00:19:55.500
I'm quite greedy, I'm afraid.

00:19:55.500 --> 00:19:58.240
So I intend to become much, much stronger,
 as far as I can take it.

00:20:00.680 --> 00:20:04.860
And so, I hope you'll 
make your comeback soon.

00:20:10.740 --> 00:20:13.240
Wait, is the person you want to beat...

00:20:14.020 --> 00:20:19.530
I had never been disappointed by how strong 
an opponent seemed before.

00:20:31.970 --> 00:20:35.750
It's true that I won the Spring Tennoushou.

00:20:36.110 --> 00:20:40.230
Thirty-two hundred meters on turf... 
A distance I specialize in.

00:20:41.440 --> 00:20:45.590
But we haven't competed over the 
distance you specialize in yet.

00:20:45.590 --> 00:20:47.850
My distance?

00:20:47.850 --> 00:20:50.760
I'm sure there's a distance 
that you're best suited to,

00:20:50.760 --> 00:20:53.270
much like how I'm called a stayer.

00:20:53.930 --> 00:20:56.100
A distance I'm good at...

00:20:56.100 --> 00:20:59.850
It wouldn't be fair unless we 
raced over that distance, too.

00:21:00.360 --> 00:21:02.670
As a horse girl of the Mejiro family,

00:21:02.670 --> 00:21:05.720
I cannot claim glory unless 
my victory is complete.

00:21:07.120 --> 00:21:10.360
Next time, I will crush you, 
at your best distance.

00:21:10.840 --> 00:21:14.780
So wipe that hollow look off your face.

00:21:15.290 --> 00:21:19.960
Your desire for victory, the same one 
every horse girl has, isn't gone, is it?

00:21:21.290 --> 00:21:27.520
From this moment on, I'd be glad to 
to run so as to be a goal for you.

00:21:38.310 --> 00:21:40.240
What's that look for?

00:21:40.240 --> 00:21:43.540
Well, since you're so set on it,
 I guess I could race you.

00:21:43.540 --> 00:21:45.950
But you might end up crying when you lose!

00:21:45.950 --> 00:21:49.710
I could easily say the same to you.

00:21:52.150 --> 00:21:54.620
I'm not gonna lose again!

00:21:55.300 --> 00:21:56.890
Challenge accepted.

00:21:59.830 --> 00:22:03.710
Incidentally, would you like 
to have your injury examined?

00:22:03.710 --> 00:22:06.890
Oh, have you forgotten how 
skilled my family's doctor is?

00:22:06.890 --> 00:22:08.830
I couldn't if I wanted to!

00:22:08.830 --> 00:22:11.260
U-Uh, let go!

00:22:11.260 --> 00:22:13.420
The preparations are already complete.

00:22:13.420 --> 00:22:14.970
D-Don't tell me...

00:22:14.970 --> 00:22:16.290
I'm the doctor.

00:22:16.290 --> 00:22:17.690
There he is!

00:22:17.930 --> 00:22:21.160
Please, enjoy a special course 
of the Mejiro family's treatment.

00:22:21.810 --> 00:22:23.680
Now, let's move along.

00:22:23.680 --> 00:22:25.690
W-Wait a second!

00:22:29.450 --> 00:22:32.150
Hang on! Why's he got a needle?!

00:22:32.150 --> 00:22:34.360
Because I'm the young lady's doctor.

00:22:34.360 --> 00:22:36.950
What is even happening?!
